        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "In code, that's the whole rotation. Save y and T three. Make z y's right child, and T three z's left. Then update the heights: z first, because it's now below y. Return y, so the caller can link the new subtree root. Rotate left is the mirror image.",
          "props": {
            "title": "The <em>code</em>",
            "file": "rotate.cpp",
            "tag": "C++",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 26,
            "width": 1150,
            "code": "Node* rotateRight(Node* z) {     // z is left-heavy\n    Node* y  = z->left;\n    Node* T3 = y->right;\n    y->right = z;                   // z moves down, right\n    z->left  = T3;                  // T3 changes parent\n    update(z);                      // z first: it's lower now\n    update(y);\n    return y;                       // the new subtree root\n}",
            "highlights": [
