        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "Insert is a normal search tree insert, plus rebalance on the way back up. Rebalance updates the height and checks the balance factor. When it's left-heavy, and the left child leans right, rotate it left first, then rotate right. Right-heavy is the mirror. An insert needs at most one of these fixes. A delete can need one at every level, O of log n rotations.",
          "props": {
            "title": "rebalance()",
            "file": "avl.cpp",
            "tag": "C++",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 20,
            "width": 1250,
            "code": "Node* rebalance(Node* n) {\n    update(n);\n    int b = bf(n);                                // height(left) - height(right)\n    if (b > 1) {                                  // left-heavy\n        if (bf(n->left) < 0)                      // LR: zigzag\n            n->left = rotateLeft(n->left);\n        return rotateRight(n);                    // LL\n    }\n    if (b < -1) {                                 // right-heavy\n        if (bf(n->right) > 0)                     // RL: zigzag\n            n->right = rotateRight(n->right);\n        return rotateLeft(n);                     // RR\n    }\n    return n;\n}\nNode* insert(Node* n, int v) {\n    if (!n) return new Node(v);\n    if (v < n->val)      n->left  = insert(n->left, v);\n    else if (v > n->val) n->right = insert(n->right, v);\n    return rebalance(n);                          // on the way back up\n}",
            "highlights": [
              {
                "at": "Insert",
                "lines": "16-20",
                "note": "BST insert, rebalance on the way up"
              },
              {
                "at": "checks",
                "lines": "2-3",
                "note": "Balance factor"
              },
              {
                "at": "leans",
                "lines": "4-7",
                "note": "LR: straighten, then LL"
              },
              {
                "at": "mirror",
                "lines": "9-12",
                "note": "RL and RR: the mirror"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
